  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "A bag has $4$ tiles labeled with two, $5$ tiles labeled with seven, and $3$ tiles labeled with fifteen. If one tile is randomly drawn from the bag, what is its expected value? Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn tile. Then the support is $S={2,7,15}.$\n\nIn the bag, there are $5$ tiles labeled with seven, $4$ tiles labeled with two, and $3$ tiles labeled with fifteen (twelve tiles in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2) & =\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ P(7) & =\\frac{5}{12} \\\\ P(15) & =\\frac{3}{12}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+7\\cdot f(7)+15\\cdot f(15) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{3})+7(\\frac{5}{12})+15(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{35}{12}+\\frac{15}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{12}+\\frac{35}{12}+\\frac{45}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{8+35+45}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{88}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
